{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>בפרוח</b> (when they flourish) — these are those who prosper in the land." "<b>And the sense of להשמדם</b> (to destroy them) — this is their end, as in: יחד כסיל ובער יאבדו (together the fool and the brutish perish), as I explained. Or that HaShem repays good to the wicked in this world for a good deed he did, to destroy him in his end, as written in the Torah of HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 92, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:02.818885046Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}